{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456536-archaic-sorcery-for-m20-on-2021","id":1456536,"title":"Archaic Sorcery for M20 on 2021?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-10T09:53:56-07:00","id":1456536,"title":"Archaic Sorcery for M20 on 2021?","content":"Folks,y'know the archaic sorcery system depicted starting on page 152 of V20 True Black Hand?<br /> Could such magic still be used in-setting on the modern age of Mages? Do the old magic of the dark ages,the pillars and foundations still can be used in 2021?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T10:55:31-07:00","id":1456540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456536-archaic-sorcery-for-m20-on-2021#post1456536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Folks,y'know the archaic sorcery system depicted starting on page 152 of V20 True Black Hand?<br /> Could such magic still be used in-setting on the modern age of Mages? Do the old magic of the dark ages,the pillars and foundations still can be used in 2021?</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally wouldn\u2019t recommend it for PCs in a game where other PCs are using spheres. The biggest benefit of those rules are that it was a way to sneak us the Chakravanti\u2019s DA Mage Foundation and Pillars.<br /> <br /> Now if you want to to use DA Mage rules only in the modern setting instead of spheres, that is a whole other conversation, and workable though you obviously have a lot more groups to writeup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T11:18:41-07:00","id":1456541,"title":"","content":"Despite sharing similar names the Spheres of the game rules are not the same as the in-universe Spheres. In universe there are countless contradictory explanations of magic. At the table, though, everyone should be using largely the same system*. If you are using the Sphere system, every player of an Awakened Mage should be using it, even those playing characters who actively reject Spheres. <br /> <br /> *variant Spheres are a thing, but they largely play the same way.<br /> <br /> So the philosophies and teachings of the old ways can still be used, yes, but you'd still use Spheres to calculate and resolve the actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T11:21:52-07:00","id":1456542,"title":"","content":"The single biggest issue in my opinion is the dice pool. M20 magic has a dice pool based off of Arete, running from 1 to 10 but tending heavily toward the low end. Archaic magic has a nice pool based off of foundation + pillar, both of which can go up to five. The overall range is 2 to 10, and at the low end they tend to be considerably larger. Often twice as big. There's also the fact that pillars can exceed foundation; though you have to pay quintessence if they do.<br /> <br /> That said, I do like the idea of the largely stick in the mud disparates still using archaic magic today, having never bought into the Spheres. For them, I'd use M20's rules for Magick, with the apple exception of replacing the Spheres with Pillars when determining whether or not you have enough know-how to attempt an Effect. Let Foundation go ask the way up to 10, just like Arete; base the dice pool strictly on Foundation, just like Arete; and cap the Pillars to no more than Foundation, just like Arete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T12:26:33-07:00","id":1456544,"title":"","content":"thanks everyonee","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T12:29:45-07:00","id":1456545,"title":"","content":"just to be sure i understand,while mechanicallly it is not the best idea.<br /> in-setting,it is doable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T12:35:36-07:00","id":1456546,"title":"","content":"In setting, you have always had groups that do not recognize the spheres. The original write up for the Sisters of Hypollyta specifically mentioned that they don't recognize the Spheres, or even the division between awakened and sleeper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T12:39:41-07:00","id":1456547,"title":"","content":"gotchaaaaa","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T13:22:16-07:00","id":1456549,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think Archaic Sorcery could make for an interesting alternative to sorcery paths. They're comparable in power to a Sphere mage but without the ability to truly branch out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T11:25:11-07:00","id":1457219,"title":"","content":"Pillar magic as used in v20 is basically just a pillar made from 4 specialized spheres (v20 called them keywords) and some tiering with what could be done with them, so you'd have Pillar: Elements (keywords: Fire, Water, Earth, Air). You got a foci specialty at Foundation 4 and a keyword specialty at Path 4. the formula went like this:<br /> <br /> Pillars<br /> -in general a pillar does the following at each dot of power, often reduce the requirement for self targeting effects or if it requires quintessence<br /> \u2022 Awareness of the keywords of a pillar, Protection against passive keyword effects (ex: heat but not fire)<br /> \u2022\u2022 add bonuses or penalties related to keywords, call (but not compel or create) keywords, inflict bashing damage, interact with keywords directly (ex: touching ghosts)<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 manipulate a keyword, inflict lethal damage, summon, ban or trap a keyword, damage/destroy keywords, embody or traverse the keyword, make another interact with a keyword directly<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 transform a keyword completely, command or control a keyword, transcend mortal limits, make another embody or traverse a keyword<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 unleash widespread keyword, transcend divinely imposed limits, make massive incontestable transformations","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26927,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26927-sylvanvixen","user":"SylvanVixen","date":". 08-19-2021, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26927-sylvanvixen","name":"SylvanVixen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T12:10:02-07:00","id":1457221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SylvanVixen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456536-archaic-sorcery-for-m20-on-2021?p=1457219#post1457219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pillar magic as used in v20 is basically just a pillar made from 4 specialized spheres (v20 called them keywords) and some tiering one what could be done with them, so you'd have Pillar: Elements (keywords: Fire, Water, Earth, Air). You got a foci specialty at Foundation 4 and a keyword specialty at Path 4. the formula went like this:<br /> <br /> Pillars<br /> -in general a pillar does the following at each dot of power, often reduce the requirement for self targeting effects or if it requires quintessence<br /> \u2022 Awareness of the keywords of a pillar, Protection against passive keyword effects (ex: heat but not fire)<br /> \u2022\u2022 add bonuses or penalties related to keywords, call (but not compel or create) keywords, inflict bashing damage, interact with keywords directly (ex: touching ghosts)<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 manipulate a keyword, inflict lethal damage, summon, ban or trap a keyword, damage/destroy keywords, embody or traverse the keyword, make another interact with a keyword directly<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 transform a keyword completely, command or control a keyword, transcend mortal limits, make another embody or traverse a keyword<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 unleash widespread keyword, transcend divinely imposed limits, make massive incontestable transformations</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that from Guide to the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T13:04:19-07:00","id":1457225,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it was my analysis of how the Idran pillars worked and what they did at each rating so I could make more if I wanted while I was on a design kick. I posted that here awhile ago under a previous username.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26927,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26927-sylvanvixen","user":"SylvanVixen","date":". 08-19-2021, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26927-sylvanvixen","name":"SylvanVixen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}